<section class="faq g-paper">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="faq-top">
      <div class="faq-aside">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-v9-reveal><span class="tick">\</span> 03 · Before you write</div>
        <h2 style="--d:60ms" data-v9-reveal>Six things people ask first.</h2>
        <div class="faq-ask" style="--d:180ms" data-v9-reveal>
          <p class="faq-ask-q">Still unsure?</p><a href="#write"
            >Write anyway <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
          >
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list" style="--d:120ms" data-v9-reveal>
        <details class="faq-item" name="contact-faq" open="">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>How fast do you actually reply?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                Inside a day, whichever side you’re on. If it’s urgent, say so in the first line and it moves to the
                top.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="contact-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"><span>What does it cost?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                For recruitment, a percentage of the hire’s annual CTC, due only when you hire. Some clients prefer a
                monthly retainer with a Tribera recruiter inside their team. Interview as a service is a fee per
                interview, plus a success fee if you hire. We quote for the role after the first call.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="contact-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>Is there ever a fee for candidates?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a"><div><p>No. Not now, not when you’re placed, not ever.</p></div></div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="contact-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>Do you work outside India?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                Yes. We run searches for GCCs and global teams hiring into India, and for India-based teams hiring
                elsewhere. Our people sit in Pune and Bengaluru.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="contact-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>Can you handle remote and hybrid roles?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"
            ></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                Yes, and the bar is set differently for them. Remote roles weight written communication and
                self-direction more heavily, and the scorecard says so.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details class="faq-item" name="contact-faq">
          <summary class="faq-q"
            ><span>What should I put in the message?</span><span class="faq-ic" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary
          >
          <div class="faq-a">
            <div>
              <p>
                The role, the level, how long it’s been open and what you’ve already tried. Four sentences is plenty.
                We’d rather have the honest version than a polished brief.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
